1
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:09,433
Since that day, Hayama
has stopped contacting me.

2
00:00:13,433 --> 00:00:17,033
Miyama University, 2nd year, winter

3
00:00:23,067 --> 00:00:26,267
Hey, what are you doing after this?

4
00:00:27,367 --> 00:00:29,467
Apparently Minami got a boyfriend.

5
00:00:30,533 --> 00:00:32,467
Why'd you turn her down? What a waste.

6
00:00:33,667 --> 00:00:35,567
I didn't exactly turn her down.

7
00:00:37,200 --> 00:00:39,667
Sounds like the one that
got away was a big catch.

8
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:46,467
It's better to date someone
who'll take you seriously.

9
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:49,267
And you couldn't do that for her.

10
00:00:51,733 --> 00:00:53,167
Yeah, pretty much.

11
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:58,100
I'll introduce you to another
girl who's interested in you.

12
00:00:58,900 --> 00:01:01,933
The more people you meet, the better
your odds of finding someone serious.

13
00:01:02,267 --> 00:01:06,000
There are tons of girls who
want an introduction to you.

14
00:01:07,267 --> 00:01:09,167
Give me a break.

15
00:01:29,167 --> 00:01:32,900
Hey, Midori, your phone's going
off like crazy. Are you okay?

16
00:01:34,833 --> 00:01:37,367
Ah... well...

17
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:40,200
Oh, so you're popular?

18
00:01:41,400 --> 00:01:43,433
Not by choice.

19
00:01:45,167 --> 00:01:48,767
The one person I actually want
to hear from never contacts me.

20
00:01:49,267 --> 00:01:51,333
Oh, Midori.

21
00:01:52,200 --> 00:01:52,700
Hello.

22
00:01:53,433 --> 00:01:55,600
Thanks for coming by again.

23
00:01:56,033 --> 00:01:57,200
What brings you in today?

24
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,867
Our coming-of-age ceremony is coming up.

25
00:01:59,867 --> 00:02:02,667
We're getting the high school
track club together then, too.

26
00:02:02,667 --> 00:02:05,167
The ceremony's finally here.

27
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:07,933
Ao has grown up too.

28
00:02:07,933 --> 00:02:10,866
That's right. He's all grown up.

29
00:02:12,100 --> 00:02:15,500
How lovely. Your teacher will be so happy.

30
00:02:17,367 --> 00:02:19,267
Oh, by the way, Midori.

31
00:02:19,267 --> 00:02:22,033
There's a class reunion before the
club get-together. Are you going?

32
00:02:23,433 --> 00:02:25,600
Yeah, that's the plan. Oh, I see.

33
00:02:26,567 --> 00:02:28,033
Then I think I'll go too.

34
00:02:29,567 --> 00:02:31,400
You must be looking
forward to the ceremony.

35
00:02:32,067 --> 00:02:34,200
You might even see people
you haven't met in a while.

36
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:36,767
True.

37
00:02:37,667 --> 00:02:38,167
I guess so.

38
00:02:40,333 --> 00:02:42,567
About the flowers for our teacher...

39
00:02:44,267 --> 00:02:45,267
How about something like these?

40
00:02:45,867 --> 00:02:47,033
They're pretty.

41
00:02:48,400 --> 00:02:49,367
Not bad, right?

42
00:02:49,600 --> 00:02:50,667
They look so warm.

43
00:02:54,433 --> 00:03:01,267
♪ Closing my eyes, I
breathe deep to calm down ♪

44
00:03:01,767 --> 00:03:05,900
♪ I put on a straight face
and hide my racing heart ♪

45
00:03:05,900 --> 00:03:09,400
♪ A blue impulse pierces my chest ♪

46
00:03:09,833 --> 00:03:10,667
♪ Look at you ♪

47
00:03:10,667 --> 00:03:14,500
♪ Before I know it, it's only
you. I'm fallin' for you ♪

48
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:21,433
♪ So vague, the distance never closes.
You're an answer I can't solve ♪

49
00:03:21,433 --> 00:03:25,000
♪ Ah, my whole heart was stolen ♪

50
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:26,333
♪ Crush on you ♪

51
00:03:29,500 --> 00:03:32,967
♪ My whole heart was stolen ♪

52
00:03:32,967 --> 00:03:34,833
♪ Crush on you ♪

53
00:03:41,067 --> 00:03:41,800
Wow!

54
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:43,667
It's been so long!

55
00:03:47,867 --> 00:03:49,067
Looking for someone?

56
00:03:49,767 --> 00:03:51,100
Nah, not really.

57
00:03:52,367 --> 00:03:52,867
Huh?

58
00:03:53,533 --> 00:03:54,233
Hey, Sudo!

59
00:03:54,600 --> 00:03:55,133
Yamamuro!

60
00:03:55,467 --> 00:03:56,567
It's been ages!

61
00:03:58,400 --> 00:03:59,833
Hey, long time no see.

62
00:03:59,833 --> 00:04:01,167
Haven't seen you since graduation, right?

63
00:04:01,367 --> 00:04:01,967
How've you been?

64
00:04:02,333 --> 00:04:03,500
Not bad.

65
00:04:04,267 --> 00:04:05,900
So you're coming to the track club
get-together after this, right?

66
00:04:06,300 --> 00:04:08,800
Yeah, I'll be there. We don't go
home until we know our limits.

67
00:04:08,800 --> 00:04:10,900
That's the track club tradition.

68
00:04:12,367 --> 00:04:15,667
- Who came up with that weird rule?
- Ao!

69
00:04:19,166 --> 00:04:21,767
We're talking about a class
get-together after this.

70
00:04:21,767 --> 00:04:24,900
Ao, you should come too.
Karaoke, apparently.

71
00:04:24,900 --> 00:04:25,800
Yeah, let's go.

72
00:04:29,067 --> 00:04:32,100
- Yamamura, let's go get drinks.
- Sure.

73
00:04:35,967 --> 00:04:36,767
Maracas!

74
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:39,300
I just picked these up.

75
00:04:39,833 --> 00:04:41,400
Maracas are really in right now, huh?

76
00:04:41,867 --> 00:04:43,433
Let's play together.

77
00:04:44,100 --> 00:04:45,667
Then I'll do the tambourine.

78
00:04:45,667 --> 00:04:47,500
Okay, so Ao's on maracas.

79
00:04:47,500 --> 00:04:49,900
Ao on maracas at karaoke!

80
00:04:49,900 --> 00:04:51,367
- Let's do it.
- Sure.

81
00:04:54,733 --> 00:04:55,600
Ready?

82
00:04:56,067 --> 00:04:57,067
Cheers!

83
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:01,500
Ao.

84
00:05:02,300 --> 00:05:05,100
I saw Yamamura. Did you talk to him?

85
00:05:05,500 --> 00:05:07,600
No, he was with his club friends.

86
00:05:07,600 --> 00:05:08,200
Huh?

87
00:05:08,800 --> 00:05:10,500
So what? That doesn't matter.

88
00:05:11,933 --> 00:05:15,300
- It'd only bother him if I talked to him.
- Huh?

89
00:05:15,433 --> 00:05:16,633
Why would you say that?

90
00:05:19,833 --> 00:05:21,933
Did something happen with Yamamura?

91
00:05:24,767 --> 00:05:27,267
Midori...

92
00:05:28,400 --> 00:05:30,733
- He probably has a girlfriend now.
- What?

93
00:05:33,733 --> 00:05:34,833
So it's fine now.

94
00:05:35,567 --> 00:05:37,367
Someone knock Yamamura out!

95
00:05:37,467 --> 00:05:39,867
Arisa, calm down!

96
00:05:41,000 --> 00:05:42,667
Midori didn't do anything wrong.

97
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:45,833
Besides, I figured from the
start that Midori wasn't like me.

98
00:05:47,700 --> 00:05:48,367
I know, but...

99
00:05:48,833 --> 00:05:51,000
- But you two used to meet up alone.
- Yeah.

100
00:05:51,400 --> 00:05:54,000
I thought he really cared about you, Ao.

101
00:05:55,400 --> 00:05:56,500
Midori thinks of me

102
00:05:56,833 --> 00:05:58,667
as a good friend.

103
00:06:00,267 --> 00:06:01,933
So if he's got a girlfriend now,

104
00:06:02,733 --> 00:06:04,400
I figured I should stop seeing him.

105
00:06:15,667 --> 00:06:17,567
Cutting ties on your own like that

106
00:06:19,400 --> 00:06:20,633
has to be lonely.

107
00:06:25,033 --> 00:06:28,267
Can you really move on that way, Ao?

108
00:06:33,767 --> 00:06:36,267
Even if you keep your distance
because loving him hurts,

109
00:06:36,733 --> 00:06:38,500
it won't stop hurting.

110
00:06:51,733 --> 00:06:53,500
Seriously, you...

111
00:06:54,500 --> 00:06:56,733
Come on, man.

112
00:07:04,833 --> 00:07:06,733
I'm home.

113
00:07:32,800 --> 00:07:38,067
Come to think of it,
the piano was the same.

114
00:07:52,433 --> 00:07:54,567
I just can't move forward.

115
00:08:01,900 --> 00:08:07,500
Even apart, it still hurts just as much.

116
00:08:20,167 --> 00:08:21,500
It's no use.

117
00:08:27,333 --> 00:08:29,833
I'm still completely in love with him.

118
00:08:44,767 --> 00:08:45,500
Okay.

119
00:09:09,933 --> 00:09:11,300
Welcome!

120
00:09:25,833 --> 00:09:26,567
Hey.

121
00:09:28,967 --> 00:09:29,467
Hi.

122
00:09:45,267 --> 00:09:45,900
You know,

123
00:09:48,167 --> 00:09:49,567
I decided I shouldn't let
my relationship with Midori

124
00:09:51,833 --> 00:09:54,167
turn out like the piano.

125
00:09:59,700 --> 00:10:01,700
I'd regret it forever.

126
00:10:07,467 --> 00:10:09,367
So thank you for inviting me today.

127
00:10:15,300 --> 00:10:17,400
Wait, I have no idea what you mean.

128
00:10:17,400 --> 00:10:18,300
I feel so much better.

129
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:21,000
I'm getting the omurice.

130
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:22,433
Who said you could feel
better on your own?

131
00:10:22,433 --> 00:10:23,767
What are you having, Midori?

132
00:10:23,767 --> 00:10:25,567
Stop moving the conversation along!

133
00:10:25,567 --> 00:10:27,200
Excuse me, can we order?

134
00:10:27,233 --> 00:10:28,700
- I'll eat, but still...
- Yes, coming!

135
00:10:31,800 --> 00:10:34,500
One chicken curry and one omurice, please.

136
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:35,500
Okay.

137
00:10:36,833 --> 00:10:37,333
Huh?

138
00:10:40,233 --> 00:10:41,000
You don't remember?

139
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:45,767
Well, the whole track
club went to Yoshida's,

140
00:10:45,767 --> 00:10:47,800
and I remember up until the after-party,

141
00:10:50,467 --> 00:10:53,933
but after that it's just a vague blur.

142
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:58,100
Surprising. I thought you
could hold your liquor, Midori.

143
00:10:58,100 --> 00:11:00,067
I can.

144
00:11:02,667 --> 00:11:05,433
I just got a bad buzz, that's all.

145
00:11:06,933 --> 00:11:09,100
Oh, a bad buzz?

146
00:11:09,633 --> 00:11:10,467
That's surprising too.

147
00:11:14,100 --> 00:11:15,600
And whose fault do you think that is?

148
00:11:17,167 --> 00:11:18,267
What do you mean?

149
00:11:20,867 --> 00:11:22,300
Never mind.

150
00:11:33,300 --> 00:11:34,600
Hey...

151
00:11:37,333 --> 00:11:39,633
Once things get busier,

152
00:11:41,533 --> 00:11:43,767
we won't be able to meet often, right?

153
00:11:44,200 --> 00:11:44,700
Right.

154
00:11:49,267 --> 00:11:49,767
So...

155
00:11:52,333 --> 00:11:54,367
we won't be able to meet up much.

156
00:11:57,433 --> 00:11:58,067
Got it.

157
00:11:58,933 --> 00:12:00,367
I want to see you more, too.

158
00:12:02,267 --> 00:12:03,767
What do you mean, "too"?

159
00:12:04,267 --> 00:12:06,067
It sounds like I'm the
one who wants to see you.

160
00:12:06,067 --> 00:12:08,267
Huh? Isn't that what we
were just talking about?

161
00:12:08,567 --> 00:12:10,900
Don't get cocky, you idiot.

162
00:12:10,900 --> 00:12:12,000
I'm not.

163
00:12:12,767 --> 00:12:13,500
Yeah, yeah.

164
00:12:14,833 --> 00:12:16,033
See you around.

165
00:12:17,867 --> 00:12:18,967
Yeah, see you.

166
00:12:29,933 --> 00:12:30,933
Midori...

167
00:12:32,267 --> 00:12:33,867
Even if you get a
girlfriend, nothing changes.

168
00:12:38,867 --> 00:12:41,867
University, 4th year, summer

169
00:12:43,567 --> 00:12:44,800
Yo.

170
00:12:45,233 --> 00:12:46,900
Hey. Coming back from an interview?

171
00:12:47,167 --> 00:12:47,667
How'd it go?

172
00:12:48,967 --> 00:12:50,033
So-so.

173
00:12:50,833 --> 00:12:53,333
Always so relaxed. As expected.

174
00:12:53,933 --> 00:12:55,533
You've already got an
offer, haven't you, Iida?

175
00:12:56,133 --> 00:12:56,967
Did she get one too?

176
00:12:57,200 --> 00:13:00,300
Yeah. Didn't I tell you
she's in the same industry?

177
00:13:00,833 --> 00:13:01,733
Oh, we broke up, though.

178
00:13:02,233 --> 00:13:03,133
Again?

179
00:13:04,233 --> 00:13:06,833
Our schedules didn't line up.

180
00:13:07,733 --> 00:13:11,600
Well, I can't see you
putting a girlfriend first.

181
00:13:11,600 --> 00:13:12,833
Who are you calling heartless?

182
00:13:12,833 --> 00:13:14,700
I never said that.

183
00:13:15,100 --> 00:13:19,000
By the way, a girl in my seminar asked me
to introduce you again. What do you think?

184
00:13:21,433 --> 00:13:24,167
No way. Job hunting and my
thesis are all I can handle.

185
00:13:24,167 --> 00:13:26,867
You need a break. Even just
texting would be fine.

186
00:13:26,867 --> 00:13:29,667
I don't have time for that. See you.

187
00:13:35,933 --> 00:13:39,300
But don't you still grab meals
with that guy from high school?

188
00:13:42,067 --> 00:13:43,833
Ugh, I'm exhausted.

189
00:13:45,267 --> 00:13:45,967
How did it go?

190
00:13:48,667 --> 00:13:52,267
Well, I was nervous, but it went okay.

191
00:13:52,267 --> 00:13:55,267
That's great. It was your
first choice, right?

192
00:13:55,900 --> 00:13:56,400
Yeah.

193
00:14:02,067 --> 00:14:04,133
I want to see Midori.

194
00:14:07,067 --> 00:14:11,000
We haven't been able to meet at
all since job hunting got serious.

195
00:14:12,367 --> 00:14:14,833
But you two went back to having
meals together sometimes, right?

196
00:14:17,067 --> 00:14:19,767
Yeah, but it'd be unfair
to his girlfriend,

197
00:14:21,767 --> 00:14:23,567
so I'm not going to tell him how I feel.

198
00:14:25,633 --> 00:14:26,367
I see.

199
00:14:28,433 --> 00:14:28,933
But...

200
00:14:30,800 --> 00:14:32,667
even if Midori gets a girlfriend,

201
00:14:34,167 --> 00:14:36,533
my feelings for him won't change.

202
00:14:41,133 --> 00:14:44,600
Well, if you're at peace
with it, Ao, that's fine.

203
00:14:47,733 --> 00:14:51,467
After all, we'll soon be too busy
to worry about love or anything,

204
00:14:51,467 --> 00:14:55,567
- because we'll be so busy.
- Yeah.

205
00:14:55,967 --> 00:14:56,467
Ah...

206
00:14:56,967 --> 00:15:00,500
College life's almost
over. That went fast.

207
00:15:09,667 --> 00:15:10,167
Oh?

208
00:15:10,833 --> 00:15:11,933
Midori, what brings you here?

209
00:15:12,733 --> 00:15:13,900
I was in the area.

210
00:15:14,933 --> 00:15:18,567
- I got a job.
- Oh! Congratulations.

211
00:15:18,567 --> 00:15:19,733
The company you interviewed at before?

212
00:15:20,667 --> 00:15:24,033
- Yes.
- As expected of you, Midori. So capable.

213
00:15:25,900 --> 00:15:29,933
So that's what you came to hear. Nice.

214
00:15:29,933 --> 00:15:31,667
Let me give you the flowers for free.

215
00:15:31,667 --> 00:15:34,833
- It's fine, I'll pay.
- It's the thought that counts.

216
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:37,400
Please, take them.

217
00:15:38,267 --> 00:15:38,967
Thanks.

218
00:15:41,200 --> 00:15:41,933
Oh, right.

219
00:15:42,367 --> 00:15:43,633
Midori, do you have a vase?

220
00:15:44,533 --> 00:15:45,033
Want to buy one?

221
00:15:45,933 --> 00:15:48,367
Nah, I've got a beer glass.

222
00:15:49,433 --> 00:15:52,033
That's not even a vase. That's hilarious.

223
00:15:59,300 --> 00:16:01,033
Hayama got a job too, apparently.

224
00:16:01,033 --> 00:16:04,767
Oh, double the good news! Then...

225
00:16:07,367 --> 00:16:08,667
For Hayama too.

226
00:16:09,433 --> 00:16:11,633
No, there's no point in my taking them.

227
00:16:12,333 --> 00:16:13,667
Give them to him.

228
00:16:14,067 --> 00:16:16,167
We don't have plans to meet that suddenly.

229
00:16:16,167 --> 00:16:18,767
You can't just wait for plans.

230
00:16:18,767 --> 00:16:21,733
You have to go get them yourself.

231
00:16:22,800 --> 00:16:24,267
What are you talking about?

232
00:16:26,133 --> 00:16:26,833
Lately...

233
00:16:27,267 --> 00:16:28,433
haven't you two been meeting?

234
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:31,833
Not at all during job hunting.

235
00:16:32,567 --> 00:16:37,233
- And there's the thesis, too.
- Wow, college sounds tough.

236
00:16:37,767 --> 00:16:40,633
He's been going on about
his thesis every day too.

237
00:16:42,033 --> 00:16:43,667
Until we've both settled down,

238
00:16:44,533 --> 00:16:45,967
we haven't made any plans to meet.

239
00:16:47,533 --> 00:16:48,800
Oh, then,

240
00:16:49,933 --> 00:16:52,667
let's have a reunion once you graduate.

241
00:16:53,167 --> 00:16:54,200
A reunion?

242
00:16:55,567 --> 00:16:57,200
Like the coming-of-age ceremony one?

243
00:16:57,200 --> 00:16:59,967
Well, a smaller group.

244
00:17:00,567 --> 00:17:04,200
Just the people who want to meet up.

245
00:17:07,833 --> 00:17:08,900
True.

246
00:17:09,967 --> 00:17:10,933
That might be nice.

247
00:17:19,700 --> 00:17:20,867
Good morning.

248
00:17:25,300 --> 00:17:26,666
Midori...

249
00:17:29,867 --> 00:17:33,167
Midori, it's been a while.

250
00:17:35,200 --> 00:17:36,067
It's been a while.

251
00:17:38,833 --> 00:17:40,167
It feels kind of nostalgic

252
00:17:40,167 --> 00:17:41,367
to see you again.

253
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:43,100
Did you change a bit?

254
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:46,467
As if I'd change that fast.

255
00:17:48,733 --> 00:17:49,600
Did you change your part?

256
00:17:51,067 --> 00:17:51,567
Yeah.

257
00:17:51,633 --> 00:17:53,367
It looks more grown-up.

258
00:17:53,367 --> 00:17:54,567
I wanted to look cooler.

259
00:17:55,933 --> 00:17:57,167
Cool.

260
00:18:00,333 --> 00:18:01,267
Don't I look cool?

261
00:18:02,667 --> 00:18:03,167
Well,

262
00:18:03,567 --> 00:18:05,667
if anything, yes.

263
00:18:07,933 --> 00:18:08,600
What?

264
00:18:09,467 --> 00:18:12,533
- Say something.
- It's nothing.

265
00:18:13,567 --> 00:18:14,533
There you are.

266
00:18:15,700 --> 00:18:16,667
How have you been?

267
00:18:17,567 --> 00:18:19,433
You've been seeing Midori, right?

268
00:18:20,233 --> 00:18:21,300
Yeah. Huh?

269
00:18:21,567 --> 00:18:22,833
Do you two even hang out?

270
00:18:22,933 --> 00:18:25,333
- Not really.
- We're super close.

271
00:18:26,567 --> 00:18:29,033
I'm not lying. We've barely talked.

272
00:18:29,033 --> 00:18:30,500
You two are totally close.

273
00:18:30,500 --> 00:18:31,600
Why would you say that?

274
00:18:32,400 --> 00:18:35,433
All right, congratulations
on graduating, you two.

275
00:18:36,233 --> 00:18:37,833
Cheers!

276
00:18:44,500 --> 00:18:47,067
Still, since graduating high school,

277
00:18:47,067 --> 00:18:50,467
it's been four years already. Time flies.

278
00:18:50,467 --> 00:18:53,133
Ever since job hunting
started, it's been a blur.

279
00:18:53,867 --> 00:18:57,400
I was so busy I hardly remember it.

280
00:18:59,133 --> 00:18:59,633
Oh,

281
00:19:00,100 --> 00:19:01,500
by the way, Midori,

282
00:19:01,500 --> 00:19:03,600
what happened with the
girlfriend-candidate situation?

283
00:19:06,533 --> 00:19:07,033
Ah,

284
00:19:07,933 --> 00:19:09,600
I heard your college friends

285
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:13,200
keep introducing you to tons
of girls. Any progress?

286
00:19:18,933 --> 00:19:19,633
Not really.

287
00:19:20,600 --> 00:19:22,000
Nothing's come of it.

288
00:19:23,933 --> 00:19:24,433
Huh?

289
00:19:27,933 --> 00:19:30,233
Midori, you got a girlfriend, didn't you?

290
00:19:33,667 --> 00:19:35,067
No, I didn't.

291
00:19:36,300 --> 00:19:40,000
- You don't have one?
- No. Don't say it so loud.

292
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,400
Then you should have said so.

293
00:19:41,400 --> 00:19:42,833
You said she was kind and nice.

294
00:19:42,833 --> 00:19:45,200
I never said we were dating.

295
00:19:45,200 --> 00:19:47,433
But I just assumed you were.

296
00:19:47,433 --> 00:19:48,833
It never even came up.

297
00:19:48,833 --> 00:19:50,933
You never asked me anything either.

298
00:19:50,933 --> 00:19:53,333
There's no point in talking about
things you don't care about.

299
00:19:53,700 --> 00:19:56,400
There's nothing about you
I don't care about, Midori.

300
00:20:06,167 --> 00:20:07,300
You two

301
00:20:07,733 --> 00:20:10,433
should realize you both
jump to conclusions.

302
00:20:27,600 --> 00:20:29,767
I'll go get drinks.

303
00:20:34,167 --> 00:20:39,633
Aw, he's embarrassed, isn't he, Hayama?

304
00:20:40,967 --> 00:20:41,700
What?

305
00:20:43,333 --> 00:20:45,167
So that's how it was.

306
00:20:51,633 --> 00:20:54,033
You're all smiles.

307
00:21:05,167 --> 00:21:09,733
Ah, I drank a bit too much.

308
00:21:11,800 --> 00:21:14,767
It was fun, all things considered.

309
00:21:15,633 --> 00:21:16,367
Yeah.

310
00:21:22,033 --> 00:21:23,467
Let's grab a meal again.

311
00:21:24,767 --> 00:21:25,267
Okay.

312
00:21:27,700 --> 00:21:28,900
Oh, Midori.

313
00:21:36,833 --> 00:21:38,467
You'll really meet me?

314
00:21:41,933 --> 00:21:44,700
You were the one who asked
me to meet up sometimes.

315
00:21:48,000 --> 00:21:49,533
That's true, but...

316
00:21:50,700 --> 00:21:51,233
But...

317
00:22:04,333 --> 00:22:06,100
I don't know.

318
00:22:32,433 --> 00:22:35,067
Think about it before we meet next time.

319
00:22:53,833 --> 00:22:54,800
What do you mean?

320
00:23:10,167 --> 00:23:12,967
This might be the end of it.

321
00:23:12,967 --> 00:23:14,567
You're in love, aren't you?

322
00:23:18,767 --> 00:23:20,567
What should I do with this?

323
00:23:20,567 --> 00:23:24,067
Why do you always say things that test me?
